---
title: "DELETE revoke_consent (User Consent Revocation API)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: supabase = createClient()
    q_init --> q_auth: user = supabase.auth.getUser()
    q_auth --> q_unauth: user == null
    q_auth --> q_params: user != null
    q_unauth --> [*]: return 401 Unauthorized
    q_params --> q_rpc: id = params.id
    q_rpc --> q_check: rpc("delete_user_consent", consent_id=id, user_id=user.id)
    q_check --> q_error: error != null
    q_check --> q_success: error == null
    q_error --> [*]: return 500 Failed to revoke consent
    q_success --> [*]: return 200 success=true

    note right of q_auth
        INV-001: Only authenticated users may proceed past auth check
    end note

    note right of q_rpc
        INV-002: RPC enforces ownership - user can only delete own consent records (p_user_id = user.id)
        INV-003: Consent ID from URL path parameter must reference an existing record
    end note

    note right of q_error
        INV-004: All RPC failures are logged and return 500 without leaking internal details
    end note
